# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: deferred-alfe-autolisp-backend-yields-to-selector — $AUTOLISP_BACKEND conflicts with an explicit --autocad / --bricscad instead of yielding
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-alfe-autolisp-backend-yields-to-selector
#+DATE: 2026-11-14

* Context

Found while implementing =cli-option-environment-defaults= (alfe 2.4.9),
which deliberately left alfe's own pre-seeded variables alone.

* Problem

=RESOLVE-BACKEND='s docstring (=autolisp-front-end/source/cli.lisp=) states
the order: "1. Explicit --bricscad / --autocad / --clautolisp wins. ... 3.
Otherwise, $AUTOLISP_BACKEND supplies the legacy default." But
=APPLY-ENV-DEFAULTS= copies =$AUTOLISP_BACKEND= into the backend slot BEFORE
argv is parsed, and the selectors' handler (=%SET-BACKEND-CHECKED=) treats an
already-set slot as a second selector:

#+begin_example
$ AUTOLISP_BACKEND=bricscad alfe --no-init --autocad --dry-run -x 1
alfe: --autocad: Conflicting backend selectors (:BRICSCAD vs :AUTOCAD)
#+end_example

(observed with the installed alfe 2.4.2; the 2.4.9 code is unchanged here.)
The explicit selector should win, as documented.

* Proposal

Stop pre-seeding the backend slot: tag the three selectors with an
environment group (as 2.4.9 did for =ALFE_CAD=, group =:cad=) or let
=RESOLVE-BACKEND= consult =$AUTOLISP_BACKEND= only when the slot is still
NIL -- which its step 3 already describes. Keep a real conflict
(=--autocad --bricscad= on one command line) an error.

* Acceptance criteria

- =AUTOLISP_BACKEND=bricscad alfe --autocad= selects AutoCAD; a test asserts
  it.
- =AUTOLISP_BACKEND=bricscad alfe= alone still selects BricsCAD.
- =alfe --autocad --bricscad= is still a usage error.
